Triangle $ABC$ has base $AC = 3\sqrt{3}$ and height $BK = 3\sqrt{3}$, so $$[ABC] =\frac12(3\sqrt{3})(3\sqrt{3}) = \boxed{9}$$ square units. </think> <answer> 9 </answer>

